---
import Header from "../components/header/header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/footer/Footer.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />

    <title>Terms & Conditions | SintraX Creations</title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Read the Terms and Conditions for participating in SintraX Creations project-building programs."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Header />

    <main>
      <section class="terms-hero">
        <div class="hero-content">
          <span class="eyebrow">SXC POLICIES</span>

          <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>

          <p>
            Please review the terms that apply to participation in SintraX
            Creations project-building programs.
          </p>

          <span class="updated">Last Updated: September 2026</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="terms-section">
        <div class="terms-container">
          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>1. Eligibility</h2>

            <p>
              SXC participation is intended for college students who are
              interested in technology and building applications, software
              products, and projects.
            </p>

            <p>
              Participants must provide accurate information during
              registration.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>2. Registration and Payment</h2>

            <ul>
              <li>The applicable program fee is <strong>₹2,999</strong>.</li>
              <li>
                The registration fee must be paid before participation is
                confirmed.
              </li>
              <li>
                Registration is completed only after the required information
                and payment process have been completed.
              </li>
              <li>
                Participants should contact SXC for payment instructions and
                clarification.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>3. Program Structure</h2>

            <ul>
              <li>The standard project-building duration is 45 days.</li>
              <li>
                Students may work as part of an assigned project team,
                depending on the project structure.
              </li>
              <li>
                Participants are expected to actively participate, collaborate,
                and complete their assigned responsibilities.
              </li>
              <li>
                SXC may extend the project timeline if additional time is
                required.
              </li>
              <li>Any such extension will not involve additional charges.</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>4. Participation and Withdrawal</h2>

            <p>
              Participants are expected to remain committed to the project
              after the project has started.
            </p>

            <p>
              Students cannot withdraw from the program after project work has
              commenced.
            </p>

            <p class="highlight">
              Due to project deadlines and team responsibilities, payments are
              non-refundable.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>5. Project Completion</h2>

            <p>Project completion depends on factors including:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>Team participation</li>
              <li>Individual contribution</li>
              <li>Communication and collaboration</li>
              <li>Timely completion of assigned tasks</li>
              <li>Adherence to project requirements and deadlines</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              SXC does not guarantee that every project will be completed,
              launched, commercialized, or converted into a startup.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>6. Project Outcomes and Guarantees</h2>

            <p>SXC participation does not guarantee:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>Employment or a job</li>
              <li>An internship</li>
              <li>A salary or stipend</li>
              <li>Revenue or financial returns</li>
              <li>Startup formation</li>
              <li>Commercial success</li>
              <li>Placement opportunities</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              SXC is designed to provide practical project-building experience
              and opportunities to develop technical, collaborative, and
              professional skills.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>7. Certificates</h2>

            <p>
              Participants may receive an SXC project certificate after
              meeting the applicable participation and completion requirements.
            </p>

            <p>Certificate eligibility may depend on:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>Participation</li>
              <li>Assigned task completion</li>
              <li>Contribution to the project</li>
              <li>Team collaboration</li>
              <li>Project deliverables</li>
              <li>Compliance with SXC requirements</li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Registration alone does not automatically guarantee a
              certificate.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>8. Use of Artificial Intelligence</h2>

            <p>
              Participants may use artificial intelligence tools as
              development or productivity aids, subject to the requirements and
              guidelines of their assigned project.
            </p>

            <p>
              Students remain responsible for understanding, reviewing, and
              contributing to the work they submit.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>9. Project Ownership and Intellectual Property</h2>

            <p>
              For projects that develop into or are intended to become
              startups:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Project code and related intellectual property are
                <strong>not automatically owned by participating students</strong>.
              </li>

              <li>
                Students may participate in a developer or other assigned
                project role.
              </li>

              <li>
                Participation does not automatically grant students ownership,
                equity, commercial rights, or intellectual-property rights in a
                project.
              </li>

              <li>
                Ownership, usage rights, responsibilities, and other related
                arrangements may vary depending on the project.
              </li>

              <li>
                Participants should contact SXC for further details and
                clarification before participating in a relevant project.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>10. Student Responsibilities</h2>

            <p>Participants agree to:</p>

            <ul>
              <li>Provide accurate registration information.</li>
              <li>Respect other participants and team members.</li>
              <li>
                Complete assigned responsibilities honestly and responsibly.
              </li>
              <li>
                Avoid plagiarism, unauthorized copying, and misuse of
                third-party content.
              </li>
              <li>Respect project confidentiality where applicable.</li>
              <li>Follow project instructions and communication guidelines.</li>
              <li>
                Avoid activities that may harm SXC, its members, partners, or
                other participants.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>11. Changes to the Program</h2>

            <p>
              SXC may make reasonable changes to project assignments, timelines,
              workflows, communication methods, or program procedures when
              necessary.
            </p>

            <p>
              Participants will be informed of significant changes through the
              official communication channels where applicable.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>12. Communication</h2>

            <p>
              For questions regarding registration, payment, project ownership,
              participation, or other program details, participants may contact
              SXC through the following channels:
            </p>

            <div class="contact-box">
              <p>
                <strong>Email:</strong>
                <a href="mailto:sintraxcreations@gmail.com">
                  sintraxcreations@gmail.com
                </a>
              </p>

              <p>
                <strong>WhatsApp:</strong>
                <a
                  href="https://api.whatsapp.com/send?phone=919490354451"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  +91 9490354451
                </a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="policy-card">
            <h2>13. Acceptance of Terms</h2>

            <p>
              By submitting the registration form and proceeding with payment,
              the participant confirms that they have read, understood, and
              agreed to these Terms &amp; Conditions.
            </p>

            <p>
              If a participant does not agree with these terms, they should not
              proceed with registration or payment.
            </p>
          </article>

          <div class="policy-footer">
            <p>
              If you need clarification about any of these terms, please
              contact the SXC team before registering.
            </p>

            <a href="/join" class="cta-button">Return to Registration</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #f4f8fc;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    color: #172b3d;
  }

  .terms-hero {
    position: relative;
    padding: 155px 24px 90px;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: white;
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 85% 20%,
        rgba(24, 213, 232, 0.16),
        transparent 30%
      ),
      linear-gradient(135deg, #071a2b, #0b263d);
  }

  .terms-hero::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 1px,
        transparent 1px
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 1px,
        transparent 1px
      );
    background-size: 42px 42px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hero-content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    width: min(900px, 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: #18d5e8;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .hero-content p {
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 24px auto 18px;
    color: #c7d7e5;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .updated {
    color: #91aabd;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .terms-section {
    padding: 75px 24px;
  }

  .terms-container {
    width: min(960px, 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .policy-card {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    padding: 32px;
    border: 1px solid #dce7f0;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgba(7, 26, 43, 0.045);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #071a2b;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: #526779;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  strong {
    color: #19364b;
  }

  .highlight {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    border-left: 4px solid #18d5e8;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #edfaff;
    color: #17445b;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-box {
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #f2f7fb;
  }

  .contact-box p {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  a {
    color: #087ca5;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .policy-footer {
    padding: 34px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: #071a2b;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .policy-footer p {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    color: #c4d4e1;
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 13px 22px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #18d5e8, #2f80ed);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    color: #ffffff;
    text-decoration: none;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .terms-hero {
      padding: 130px 20px 65px;
    }

    .terms-section {
      padding: 45px 16px;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 24px 20px;
      border-radius: 14px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }

    p,
    li {
      font-size: 0.93rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .policy-footer {
      padding: 28px 20px;
    }
  }
</style>